For this paper we use a modified $\chi^2$ likelihood function of the form: $$\begin{equation}
\ln \mathcal{L} = -0.5 f_{\rm beam}  \sum_i^{i=n} \frac{(\mathcal{M}_i - \mathcal{D}_i)^2}{\mathcal{R}_i^2}
\end{equation}$$

Under the assumption that the mass distribution is spherically symmetric, the dynamical mass enclosed within a radius, $R$, is: $$\begin{equation}
M_{\rm dyn}(R) = \frac{v_{\rm circ}^2}{G} R = 2.33 \times 10^5 v_{\rm circ}^2 R,
\label{eq:mdyn}
\end{equation}$$
